{"title":"Career Roadmap · Digital Editor","role":"Digital Editor","summary":"A Digital Editor plans, commissions, edits, publishes, optimises, and maintains content across websites, digital publications, newsletters, podcasts, social platforms, and other online channels. The role combines editorial judgement, journalism/communication, digital publishing, audience analytics, SEO, multimedia and emerging AI tools.","facts":{"Starts":"Year 1 UG · 2026","Current degree":"BA (General / Honours) — Media & Communication / Digital Media / Podcasting"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[{"period":"2026–2030","question":"What can I enter now?","output":"Editorial/content intern, digital content assistant, copy editor, social-media/content associate"},{"period":"2030–2035","question":"How should I specialise?","output":"Digital Editor, Web Editor, Content Editor, Multimedia Editor or Podcast Editor"},{"period":"2035–2040","question":"How should I evolve?","output":"Senior Digital Editor, Managing Editor, Audience Editor or Editorial Lead"},{"period":"2040–2046","question":"How can I remain relevant?","output":"Editorial Director, Head of Digital Content, Content Strategy Director or Digital Media Lead"}],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For a BA in Media & Communication / Digital Media / Podcasting, this is a strong and practical career direction."}]},{"heading":"Career-route check","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Strong alignment. The degree directly supports digital content, journalism, communication, publishing and multimedia workflows."},{"type":"p","text":"However, Digital Editor is frequently a progression role. Students commonly enter through editorial assistant, content producer, copy editor, social-content or digital publishing roles before moving into an Editor position."},{"type":"h","text":"Best employability combination:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Editorial Skills","Digital Publishing","SEO","CMS","Multime